@page "/dustbin/iframe"

<PageTitle>Dustbin · Within an iframe</PageTitle>

<div class="example">
    <h1>Dustbin &mdash; Within an iframe</h1>
    <p class="lead">
        The HTML5 backend works inside an iframe because BlazorDnd listens to the native drag
        events of whatever document it runs in. Below, a self-contained dustbin demo is hosted
        in its own iframe document &mdash; dragging works entirely within it.
    </p>

    <iframe src="dustbin/single" title="Dustbin inside an iframe"
            style="width:100%;height:420px;border:1px solid #ccc;border-radius:6px;"></iframe>

    <p style="margin-top:1rem;color:#777;">
        Note: a single <code>DndProvider</code> (and its <code>DragDropManager</code>) lives in one
        document, so dragging <em>across</em> the iframe boundary into the parent page is not
        supported by the HTML5 backend &mdash; the same limitation React DnD has without a
        cross-window backend setup.
    </p>
</div>
